[al:新概念英语第四册]
[ti:10. Creative Men]
[00:00.901]Passage 10. | 第十篇。
[00:02.325]In our new society, there is a growing dislike of original creative men. | 在我们的新社会中，人们对原创型创造性人才的厌恶与日俱增。
[00:08.080]The manipulated do not understand them. | 被操纵者不理解他们。
[00:10.890]The manipulators fear them. | 操纵者害怕他们。
[00:13.085]The tidy committeemen regard them with horror, | 整洁的委员会成员带着恐惧看待他们，
[00:16.340]knowing that no pigeon holes can be found for them. | 因为他们知道找不到适合他们的位置。
[00:19.850]We could do with a few original creative men in our political life, | 我们的政治生活确实需要一些原创性的创造性人才，
[00:24.225]if only to create some enthusiasm, release some energy. | 哪怕只是为了激发一些热情，释放一些能量。
[00:28.405]But where are they? | 但他们在哪里呢？
[00:30.330]We are asked to choose between various shades of the negative. | 我们被要求在各种负面因素之间做出选择。
[00:34.610]The engine is falling to pieces, | 引擎正在散架，
[00:36.955]while the joint owners of the car argue whether the foot brake or the hand brake should be applied. | 而汽车的共同拥有者却在争论是应该踩脚刹还是拉手刹。
[00:43.280]Notice how the cold, colorless men without ideas and with no other passion but a craving for success, | 请注意，那些冷漠、苍白、没有思想、除了渴望成功别无他求的人，
[00:50.210]get on in this society, | 是如何在社会中取得成功的，
[00:52.255]capturing one plum after another and taking the juice and taste out of them. | 他们一个接一个地攫取肥缺，却榨干了其中的精髓和味道。
[00:57.655]Sometimes you might think the machines we worship make all the chief appointments, | 有时你可能会认为我们崇拜的那些“机器”做出了所有重要的任命，
[01:02.965]promoting the human beings who seem closest to them. | 提拔那些看起来与他们最亲近的人。
[01:06.675]Between midnight and dawn, | 在午夜和黎明之间，
[01:08.885]when sleep will not come and all the old wounds begin to ache, | 当睡意全无，所有旧伤开始隐隐作痛时，
[01:12.410]I often have a nightmare vision of a future world | 我常常梦见一个可怕的未来世界，
[01:15.510]in which there are billions of people, | 那里有数十亿人，
[01:17.655]all numbered and registered, | 都被编号并注册，
[01:19.625]with not a gleam of genius anywhere, | 到处都找不到一丝天才的火花，
[01:22.025]not an original mind, | 没有一个原创的头脑，
[01:23.875]a rich personality, | 没有一个丰富的个性，
[01:25.415]on the whole packed globe. | 遍布整个拥挤的地球。
[01:27.435]The twin ideals of our time, | 我们这个时代的双重理想，
[01:29.700]organization and quantity, | 组织和数量，
[01:31.830]will have won forever. | 将永远获胜。
[01:33.985]J.B. Priestley, | J.B. 普里斯特利，
[01:36.220]Thoughts in the Wilderness. | 《荒野沉思》。